        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This silk panel has a dark green ground and a bold pattern of fanciful fruits and leaves standing in a bowl which rests on a ledge around which is hung a swag of pendant husks. The pattern is brocaded in coloured silks in reds, greens and browns, and black emphasises the outline of certain flowers. Much of the pattern is brocaded in plain and frost silver thread. The ground is woven in gros de Tours (a ribbed effect). The pattern is a point repeat (i.e. is symmetrical about a vertical axis). The repeat is 17.5 inches (47.5 centimetres) in length and 21.5 inches (58 centimetres) wide."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e10f825e-0cb4-3f13-b28b-6d42cdd938fd> .

